1. DEFINITIONS

"Affiliate" means an Organisation that controls, is controlled by, or is under
common control with another Organisation, where control means holding more than
fifty per cent of the voting rights or the power to direct management.

"Annual Gross Revenue" means the total worldwide gross revenue, turnover, or
receipts of an Organisation and all of its Affiliates, from all sources, before
deduction of costs and taxes, for its most recently completed financial year,
converted to United States dollars at the rate in effect on the last day of
that year. For an Organisation that has not completed a financial year, it
means that Organisation's annualised revenue to date. Grant income, donations,
and investment or fundraising proceeds are included only where the Organisation
recognises them as revenue in its own financial statements.

"Benefiting Organisation" means the person or Organisation receiving the
primary business benefit of a Production Use, being the one whose internal
operations, professional activities, customers, or revenue the resulting
documents serve. Where the Software is used to produce documents for or on
behalf of a client, the client is the Benefiting Organisation. Where an
Organisation embeds the Software in an application or service that it owns and
makes generally available to its own customers or users as its own product,
and not as work for a particular client, that Organisation is the Benefiting
Organisation, and its customers and users are end users under section 4.

"Commercial Production Use" means Production Use by or for a business,
government, public-sector body, or other Organisation in connection with its
internal operations, professional activities, customers, revenue-generating
activities, or other commercial benefit. It includes Production Use in a
closed-source application or service and Production Use performed for a client.

"Competing Product" means a general-purpose PDF generation library, software
development kit, toolkit, component, API, hosted service, or substantially
similar product whose primary purpose is to provide third parties with PDF
generation functionality that substitutes for the Software. A domain-specific
application or service that generates PDFs only as an ancillary part of its
own broader functionality is not a Competing Product.

"Community User" means a person or Organisation that satisfies section 2.

"Evaluation Use" means internal evaluation, development, testing, security
review, proof of concept, and non-production staging without live customer
data or live business operations.

"Licensor" means CodeFocus Limited, a company registered in England and Wales
under company number 16088203 whose registered office is at 38 Collingwood
Street, Collingwood Buildings, Newcastle, England NE1 1JF, and any successor
that validly acquires the relevant rights and makes the Software available
under the BonniePDF name.

"Organisation" means a legal entity.

"Production Use" means use in a live application, service, workflow, or
environment for the benefit of You, an Organisation, a customer, or another
third party. Production Use excludes Evaluation Use.

"Small Organisation" means a Benefiting Organisation whose Annual Gross Revenue
is less than one million United States dollars (US $1,000,000).

"Software" means the BonniePDF core PDF generation software, source code,
compiled code, documentation, and examples distributed with this licence. It
does not include BonniePDF.Signing, @bonniepdf/signing, or anything distributed
under a separate licence notice.

"You" means the individual or Organisation exercising rights under this
licence. If an individual acts for an Organisation, "You" means that
Organisation.

2. COMMUNITY ELIGIBILITY

You are a Community User only for a use described below and only while that use
continues to satisfy its conditions:

2.1 Personal and independent non-commercial use. You are an individual, or a
group of individuals acting together without forming or acting for an
Organisation, using the Software solely for personal or other non-commercial
purposes. The use must not be for an employer, client, business, profession,
trade, or other Organisation.

2.2 Charity and non-profit use. You are a registered charity or non-profit
Organisation using the Software solely in furtherance of Your charitable or
non-profit purpose, not for commercial trading and not primarily for the
commercial benefit of another person or Organisation.

2.3 Education and research. You are an accredited educational institution
using the Software solely for teaching, learning, or non-commercial academic
research. Administrative, operational, client, or other Production Use does
not qualify under this paragraph.

2.4 Open-source projects. You maintain or contribute to a project whose
complete source code is publicly available under an OSI-approved open-source
licence. The project must not be a Competing Product or be primarily developed
to meet a particular Organisation's Commercial Production Use. Funding,
sponsorship, contributions, or governance by an Organisation do not alone
disqualify an otherwise qualifying project. This paragraph permits development
and distribution of the qualifying project; it does not grant its sponsors,
contributors, maintainers, or users Commercial Production Use rights.

2.5 Evaluation. You are any person or Organisation using the Software solely
for Evaluation Use.

2.6 Small organisation use. The Benefiting Organisation is a Small
Organisation. This paragraph permits Commercial Production Use, including use
in a closed-source application or service, for so long as the Benefiting
Organisation remains a Small Organisation. It does not permit distribution of a
Competing Product, and it does not apply where any Benefiting Organisation of
the same Production Use is not a Small Organisation.

Except where paragraph 2.6 applies, Commercial Production Use is not Community
Use. It requires an applicable paid commercial licence before Production Use
begins, regardless of funding, developer count, public or private ownership, or
whether the resulting application is distributed externally.

3. COMMUNITY LICENCE GRANT

Subject to Your continuing eligibility, compliance with this licence, and use
solely for the Community purpose that qualifies under section 2, the Licensor
grants You a worldwide, non-exclusive, royalty-free, non-transferable licence
to:

(a) use and reproduce the Software;

(b) inspect, audit, modify, and create derivative works of the Software;

(c) use the Software in an application, service, workflow, or environment only
to the extent necessary for the qualifying Community purpose;

(d) permit Your employees and contractors to use the Software solely on Your
behalf for that qualifying Community purpose;

(e) deploy applications only for qualifying personal, charity, non-profit,
education, research, open-source-project, or Small Organisation use under
section 2; and

(f) distribute compiled copies only as an embedded component of (i) a
qualifying open-source project under section 2.4, or (ii) an application or
service whose use qualifies under section 2, including use permitted by
paragraph 2.6, in each case where recipients cannot reasonably use the Software
as a standalone PDF generation library. Delivering the Software to end users'
browsers or devices as part of the client-side code of a web, desktop, or
mobile application is distribution of an embedded component.

No licence key, activation, or telemetry is required for Community Use. The
absence of technical enforcement does not grant Commercial Production Use.

4. CONTRACTORS, CLIENTS, AND TRANSITIVE USERS

A contractor may perform Evaluation Use solely on behalf of a client. A
contractor may not rely on personal, charity, education, open-source, or
evaluation eligibility to provide Commercial Production Use to a client.

A contractor may not rely on its own Annual Gross Revenue under paragraph 2.6
to provide Commercial Production Use to a client. Where the Software is used
for or on behalf of a client, eligibility under paragraph 2.6 is determined by
the client's Annual Gross Revenue and not the contractor's.

End users of an application containing the Software as an embedded,
non-standalone component do not need a separate BonniePDF licence merely
because they use that application, provided the person or Organisation that
owns, operates, or distributes the application has the required rights.

5. REDISTRIBUTION AND MODIFICATIONS

You may distribute source code, modifications, or derivative works containing a
substantial part of the Software only as part of a qualifying open-source
project under section 2.4. You must:

(a) include this licence and all copyright and attribution notices;

(b) state prominently that You modified the Software, if applicable;

(c) distribute the BonniePDF-derived portion only under this licence; and

(d) not represent that the Licensor endorses or supports Your modification.

You may not sublicense the Software. Each recipient receives any rights
directly from the Licensor and only if that recipient independently qualifies
and complies with this licence.

6. RESTRICTIONS

You must not:

(a) use the Software for Commercial Production Use without an applicable paid
commercial licence;

(b) use, modify, distribute, or make the Software available as, or as a
material component of, a Competing Product;

(c) offer the Software's general-purpose PDF generation capability to third
parties as a standalone hosted API or service;

(d) remove, alter, or obscure copyright, licence, or attribution notices;

(e) use the Software or BonniePDF name in a way that implies endorsement;

(f) use the Software in violation of applicable law; or

(g) circumvent a technical measure in a separately licensed BonniePDF product.

The restrictions in this section apply to both original and modified versions
of the Software.

7. COMMERCIAL LICENCE REQUIREMENT

Evaluation may include development and testing of a proposed commercial
application, but it must not include Production Use, live customer data, live
business operations, or external distribution. Before the Software is used in
commercial production, the Benefiting Organisation must obtain a Professional,
Enterprise, Enterprise+, or other applicable paid commercial licence, unless it
is a Small Organisation and paragraph 2.6 applies to that use.

8. CHANGE IN USE

Community rights apply only while the use qualifies under section 2 and do not
vest permanently in any version. If a use becomes commercial, closed-source,
client-facing, operational, or otherwise ceases to qualify, You must obtain an
applicable paid commercial licence before that changed use begins or stop using
and distributing the Software for it.

Where eligibility rested on paragraph 2.6 and the Benefiting Organisation's
Annual Gross Revenue reaches or exceeds the threshold in the definition of
Small Organisation, You must obtain an applicable paid commercial licence
within ninety (90) days of the end of the financial year in which that first
occurred, or stop the Production Use.

No fee is due retroactively for use that was lawful Community Use.

